I'm constructing a dataset of prompts on philosophical/conceptual topics. I'd like you to write me a prompt for this dataset. I'd like the prompts to be somewhat in the weeds of things, so that models can't just regurgitate something they've seen a million times in pretraining. At the same time, I'd like the prompt to be meaningful for a model that can't search online. In particular, the prompt shouldn't ask for bibliographies, reading lists, or citations -- a model without web access could only guess at those. But they also shouldn't refer super niche theories/ideas/facts that LLMs won't have properly memorized (especially small LLMs). To comply with these two competing objectives, you'll often have to inject some sort of new / niche ideas into the prompt.

{% if domain_pages %}
This prompt is of a special kind, though: the asker shares one to three web pages, which you choose from the pages listed under the domains below. The model that answers will see the full text of the pages your prompt links to, placed ahead of your prompt, but it can't search, and it can't open any other link. So your prompt may rest on what those pages say, however niche -- that is the point of sharing them -- while anything else it needs must be in the prompt itself, as usual.

{% endif %}
