One hard rule: never quote from memory. If your prompt puts anything in quotation marks that comes from a real text, you must web_fetch a source containing the passage and copy the quote from the fetched text -- search snippets aren't good enough. If you can't fetch a usable source, don't use a verbatim quote: paraphrase without quotation marks instead. Likewise, verify titles, dates, and attributions of specific works by search if the prompt leans on them; when in doubt, write the prompt so it doesn't depend on them.

